 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "On a perpendicular coordinate plane, $A({=x1}, {=y1})$ and $B({=x2}, {=y2})$. $C$ is the midpoint of the straight segment $AB$, and $D$ is the midpoint of the straight segment $AC$. Find the two coordinates of $D$. Write your answer as $(x, y)$.",
 "solution": [
  "First find $C$, the midpoint of $AB$.",
  "$x = \\frac{{=x1} + {=paren(x2)}}{2} = {=cx}$ and $y = \\frac{{=y1} + {=paren(y2)}}{2} = {=cy}$, so $C({=cx}, {=cy})$.",
  "Now find $D$, the midpoint of $AC$, with $A({=x1}, {=y1})$ and $C({=cx}, {=cy})$.",
  "$x = \\frac{{=x1} + {=paren(cx)}}{2} = {=mx}$",
  "$y = \\frac{{=y1} + {=paren(cy)}}{2} = {=my}$",
  "So $D({=mx}, {=my})$."
 ],
 "marker": {
  "kind": "coordinates",
  "answer": "({=mx}, {=my})",
